      "text": "Let's figure out what subtracting really means. I have seven cookies. Yum! But I eat three of them. How many are left? Let's count. One, two, three, four. I have four left. That's subtraction. We started with seven, took away three, and four are left. This little line is called minus. Minus means take away. Seven takeaway three equals four. But here's something cool. Subtraction isn't just taking away. Sam has five stickers. Mia has three. How many more does Sam have? We're finding the difference. Sam has two more than Mia. Same subtraction, different question. So subtraction can mean take away or how many more. Both use minus. Now you know the secret",
